# 2. DP / Douglas–Peucker

## Primary adapted implementation

The main adapted DP implementation is:

```text
/Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams/traj-compression/batch/DP/DP_adapted.cpp
```

This is the implementation intended to compare against the repository’s canonical `N x y` format.

The core recursive implementation is:

```45:72:/Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams/traj-compression/batch/DP/DP_adapted.cpp
double calcPED(Point s, Point m, Point e) {
    double A = e.x - s.x;
    double B = s.y - e.y;
    double C = e.y * s.x - s.y * e.x;
    if (A == 0 && B == 0)
        return 0;
    return fabs((A * m.y + B * m.x + C) / sqrt(A * A + B * B));
}

vector<int> douglasPeucker(int start, int last, double epsilon) {
    double dmax = 0;
    int index = start;
    for (int i = start + 1; i < last; i++) {
        double d = calcPED(points[start], points[i], points[last]);
        if (d > dmax) {
            index = i;
            dmax = d;
        }
    }
    if (dmax > epsilon) {
        vector<int> recResults1 = douglasPeucker(start, index, epsilon);
        vector<int> recResults2 = douglasPeucker(index, last, epsilon);
        recResults1.insert(recResults1.end(), recResults2.begin(), recResults2.end());
        return recResults1;
    } else {
        return {start, last};
    }
}
```

This is the standard recursive Douglas–Peucker strategy using perpendicular distance to the line through the current segment endpoints.

## DP command-line arguments

The adapted DP binary expects exactly:

```text
DP_adapted <input.txt> <epsilon> <output.txt>
```

The parser is:

```74:84:/Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams/traj-compression/batch/DP/DP_adapted.cpp
int main(int argc, char** argv) {
    if (argc < 4) {
        cerr << "Usage: " << argv[0] << " <input.txt> <epsilon> <output.txt>" << endl;
        return 1;
    }

    string input_file = argv[1];
    double epsilon = atof(argv[2]);
    string output_file = argv[3];

    readPoints(input_file);
```

From the repository root, a direct DP run for dataset 10 would be:

```bash
cd /Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams

g++ -O3 -std=c++17 \
  traj-compression/batch/DP/DP_adapted.cpp \
  -o /tmp/DP_adapted

/tmp/DP_adapted \
  data/10/original.txt \
  200 \
  data/10/DP.txt
```

The benchmark script uses epsilon `200`:

```397:400:/Users/sinchunyeung/Simplification-of-Trajectory-Streams/scripts/benchmark.py
def run_dp(original: Path, dp_out: Path, timeout=30, mem_cap_mb=0, n_repeats=1) -> Tuple[str, float]:
    cmd = [str(DP_TOOL), str(original), "200", str(dp_out)]
    return _median_run(cmd, cwd=REPO_ROOT, timeout=timeout, mem_cap_mb=mem_cap_mb,
